1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
Thank you.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:52,600
Well, good morning again.

3
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,840
So glad that you all have joined us.

4
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:58,740
I am going to try and talk fast and stay on topic because you all are standing.

5
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:00,700
Now you know how I feel every single week.

6
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:06,080
But I am so thrilled to be a part of a church that makes something like this a priority.

7
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:12,040
There's a new, what's the word?

8
00:01:12,040 --> 00:01:14,080
Fad.

9
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:15,320
That's the word I was looking for.

10
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:17,400
There's a new fad in Christian ministry.

11
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:21,740
It pops up on my timeline all the time with pastors that I follow where they call church.

12
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:27,320
And I am, I'm convicted already because I try not to hate on our brothers and sisters in Christ.

13
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:31,100
But I call Sunday mornings a worship experience.

14
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:37,680
And as you can tell this morning, this is not an experience that we curated for you all, right?

15
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:47,480
Like this is a gathering of God's people around the things of God to agree with the things of God and to do the things of God.

16
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:55,080
And so I just want to say, like, I realize that this is not the greatest experience that we curated for you to come to.

17
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,760
But I don't think that that's what church was ever intended to be.

18
00:01:58,220 --> 00:02:05,240
And so I'm so grateful to be a part of a church that is willing to sacrifice their comfort in order to do something like this.

19
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:15,480
So we are continuing our Advent series where we light candles in anticipation for, we look back to the promises of God made and fulfilled in Jesus.

20
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:21,220
And we look forward to the future promises of God coming in the second coming.

21
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:29,100
We light these candles to show that God's love has been expressed through his first coming and will fully be expressed in his second coming.

22
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,700
And we do so with anticipation.

23
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,480
We light one candle a week.

24
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:38,180
We add to the anticipation, looking forward to light the center candle on Christmas Eve, the Christ candle,

25
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:44,120
to demonstrate that all of it, all of this is heading towards the return of Jesus.

26
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:47,920
So I'm going to light last week's candle, the hope candle.

27
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,580
Oh, yeah.

28
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:55,440
And this week's candle for love, maybe.

29
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,160
Maybe.

30
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:03,360
What are we doing?

31
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:05,800
We got it.

32
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:06,400
We got it.

33
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,840
There we go.

34
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,540
Amen.

35
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,840
Let's pray.

36
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:16,980
Father in heaven, we thank you for this day, for this opportunity to reflect on your love.

37
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:20,340
The love that chases us down, fights till we're found.

38
00:03:21,220 --> 00:03:28,100
God, and each one of the cots in this room is represented by a person that you created in your image, fearfully and wonderfully.

39
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,240
That you love deeply.

40
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:35,960
And we just hope to be some small glimpse of an expression of your love towards them this week.

41
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:36,820
May they feel it.

42
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:41,620
May they reflect on the fact that they are loved ultimately by you, their creator.

43
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:47,700
May they experience, and like Marissa said, may we experience your love as we seek to demonstrate your love to others.

44
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,260
Bless this service.

45
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,740
Be present with us.

46
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:53,740
And it's in Jesus' name I pray.

47
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,420
Amen.

48
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:57,360
I do have notes on the back of the bulletin.

49
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,000
I know some of you have become keen to that.

50
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,020
Don't get used to it because that means that I have to plan early and often.

51
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:03,700
I will do my best.

52
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:04,960
But this week I succeeded.

53
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,200
So it's there if you want to follow along.

54
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,140
And yes, it looks like a 45-minute sermon.

55
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,800
I will do my best to make it 15.

56
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:19,160
I feel like most of the time around Christmas we are usually encouraged to think happy thoughts, to focus on the positive things around us.

57
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:26,600
But just for a moment, if you would indulge me, I want you to think about the most difficult time in your life.

58
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:31,300
Try and recall the circumstances, the emotions that you were experiencing.

59
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:35,580
For most of us it won't take very long at all for us to flood back into that moment.

60
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:38,660
And some of you are mad at me for even asking you to go there.

61
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:49,360
But now I want you to think about in those most difficult, challenging moments of your life, who did you feel most loved by in those difficult seasons?

62
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:58,220
Probably isn't that hard to bring to mind the person or people that you felt most loved by in your most difficult circumstances.

63
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:06,300
And if you're anything like me, my guess is it's the people that were present with you in the midst of your circumstance.

64
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:13,580
That were willing to sacrifice their time and energy and to just sit with you in the midst of your difficult circumstances.

65
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:18,960
Text messages, cards, meals, and other acts of love are always appreciated in dark times.

66
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:21,340
So thankful for those expressions of love.

67
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:28,380
But for me, it's physical presence of people in the midst of my suffering that makes me feel most loved.

68
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:33,720
And as a pastor, I'm often called to show up in some of people's most darkest times.

69
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:44,180
And it's in these times as a pastor that I feel the most unequipped to offer anything of any value to people who are going through the most difficult time.

70
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:52,720
But as I have muscled through the difficulty and put myself in some of the people's most darkest times of their life,

71
00:05:52,720 --> 00:06:01,860
I have regularly been reminded and affirmed by the people that I showed up for that my presence is really all that is required in dark times.

72
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:04,020
I didn't have to say anything or do anything.

73
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,100
I just had to show up.

74
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:09,220
Which leads me to my main point for today's message.

75
00:06:09,220 --> 00:06:15,020
And that is this, that biblical love is most clearly demonstrated through sacrificial presence.

76
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:19,580
Biblical love is most clearly demonstrated.

77
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:21,360
It's not that it's the only way that it's demonstrated.

78
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:24,820
It's most clearly demonstrated through sacrificial presence.

79
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:32,520
Not many actions demonstrate more clearly this truth than the Advent of Jesus.

80
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:38,740
God revealed his love to the world through the presence of Christ.

81
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:46,380
The first Advent, the birth of Jesus was one of the most clearest expressions of God's love to the world.

82
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:52,680
When I think about the sacrificial presence of Christ, I don't know about you, but I typically focus on the cross.

83
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:59,460
But as I thought about this this week, that biblical love is most clearly demonstrated through sacrificial presence,

84
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:05,300
I realized that the cross is just the culmination of Christ's entire life of love towards you and me.

85
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:13,000
The incarnation in and of itself is an incredible act of love demonstrated through sacrificial presence.

86
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:18,880
1 John 4, 9 says, God showed us, demonstrated to us how much he loved us.

87
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:19,140
How?

88
00:07:19,140 --> 00:07:20,280
By dying on the cross?

89
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:20,500
No.

90
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:24,300
By sending his one and only son into the world.

91
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:31,180
The incarnation is in of itself a sacrificial act of love from God towards you and me.

92
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:34,100
That's what the word Emmanuel is all about.

93
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:35,240
Isaiah 7, 14.

94
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,640
The virgin will conceive a child.

95
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:42,680
She will give birth to a son and will call him Emmanuel, which means God with us.

96
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,780
Sacrificial presence demonstrated in the Advent of Jesus.

97
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:57,220
Lastly, Philippians chapter 2, verses 6 and 7 say this, though he was God, he did not think of equality as God as something to cling to.

98
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:01,360
Instead, he gave up sacrificially his divine privileges.

99
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,380
And what did he do instead?

100
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:06,420
He took on the humble position of a slave and was born a human being.

101
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:14,860
Sacrificial presence of the first Advent of Jesus demonstrates love towards us, towards you and me.

102
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:22,300
God revealed how much he loves us through his sacrificial presence of Christ, laying down his divinity and taking on human flesh.

103
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:26,100
His entire life is an act of love towards us.

104
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,860
But it doesn't end there.

105
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:39,480
He actually challenges those of us who would consider ourselves his followers to take up our cross and demonstrate the love that he has shown to us by being sacrificially present for others.

106
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:44,940
So God's love was revealed to us through the presence of Christ in the first Advent, the first coming of Jesus.

107
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:51,380
And God is revealing his love to the world through the presence of his Holy Spirit by us, the church.

108
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:56,600
It's the invitation for us to participate in the love that he has already demonstrated to us.

109
00:08:56,640 --> 00:09:06,700
Although God isn't physically present on earth at the moment, he has empowered his church to demonstrate his love through our sacrificial presence to the lives of those around us.

110
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:10,040
That's what this week is all about for our church.

111
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:19,960
This Watch Sunday is one of my favorite Sundays of the year because we have the opportunity to show up sacrificially and be present in the lives of those in our community who are hurting.

112
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:31,040
First John 4, 11 through 12 says, dear friends, since God loved us so much, we surely, we must, we ought to love each other.

113
00:09:31,040 --> 00:09:33,360
No one has ever seen God.

114
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,660
No one's ever seen God physically present.

115
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:38,780
None of us in this room have physically seen the presence of God.

116
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:46,960
But if we love each other, God lives in us and his love is brought to full expression in us.

117
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:54,480
People can see how much God loves the world by us as the church being willing to sacrificially be present in the lives of those who are hurting.

118
00:09:54,480 --> 00:10:01,660
If you're here and you're a follower of Jesus, your job is to model the love of Christ to others through sacrificial presence.

119
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:07,960
And my guess is that most of us would say that we could probably do a little bit better of a job.

120
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:08,640
Anybody else?

121
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:09,280
Am I the only one?

122
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:14,940
Sacrificial presence is not typically what, I've got my job review tonight.

123
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:22,300
And if I'm supposed to rank my strengths and weaknesses, I would not put sacrificial presence to those in need as my top strength.

124
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:25,560
And if you're in here and that's you, praise the Lord.

125
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:32,900
But for the rest of us, I have a couple quick practical things that we can do to better show up sacrificially for those who are in need.

126
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:38,100
Really quickly, three things that we can do to be better sacrificially present to those around us.

127
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:40,760
First, we have to be sacrificially present to God.

128
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,720
This is all from the example of Jesus.

129
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:46,400
Jesus, we read this in Luke 5 verse 16.

130
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:50,800
But Jesus often withdrew to the wilderness for prayer.

131
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:57,840
If we want to be sacrificially present to others like Jesus is sacrificially present to us, we have to follow his example.

132
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:03,620
We have to take time and intention to get alone and be with God in prayer.

133
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:09,480
Because in order for us to pour out God's love to others, we have to first receive God's love from him.

134
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:15,700
Jesus was able to be sacrificially present to others because he had a regular pattern of getting away with God.

135
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:20,700
And he had to withdraw because there was always constant needs around him.

136
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:23,660
Anybody else have constant needs around you?

137
00:11:23,660 --> 00:11:30,280
If you want to be a person of love, you have to follow the example of Jesus and sacrificially withdraw.

138
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:34,180
Say no to some things that can be said no to for a moment so that you can get away.

139
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:36,120
Maybe say no to a little bit of sleep.

140
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:39,360
I know, don't throw any rocks at me.

141
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:40,120
Do something.

142
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:44,620
In order for us to be present with God, it's often going to take us to make sacrifices.

143
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:50,220
If we want to be a people of love, we have to regularly and sacrificially be present to God.

144
00:11:50,220 --> 00:11:54,200
Second, we have to be sacrificially present to ourselves.

145
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:59,920
Now, this might seem a bit counterintuitive if you grew up in the church.

146
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:04,080
I grew up in the church and it was like sacrifice, sacrifice, sacrifice, sacrifice.

147
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:11,500
But if we look at the Old Testament Scriptures, God built in self-reflection and rest into the weekly rhythms of the Jewish people.

148
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:18,220
Because he knew that humans needed to rest in order to be present to themselves so that they could be present to others.

149
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:19,840
Mark 6.31.

150
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,300
Then Jesus said, let us go off.

151
00:12:21,300 --> 00:12:24,080
He's talking to his disciples after a long, hard week of ministry.

152
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:28,020
Let us go off by ourselves to a quiet place and rest a while.

153
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:34,500
He said this because there were so many people coming and going and Jesus and his apostles didn't even have time to eat.

154
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:37,480
Parents of toddlers in the room said, amen.

155
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:42,420
We have to be present to ourselves.

156
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:44,480
We have to have time of rest and self-reflection.

157
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:48,360
We have to know where we're at so we can love others.

158
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:52,020
It will mean we have to pay attention to how we spend our time, energy, and attention.

159
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:57,580
This past week, as I was preparing for this message, I caught myself doing what millennials have called the doom scroll.

160
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,780
Two or three times.

161
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:07,480
I'm like an hour into it and I wake up from my stupor and I'm like, what just happened?

162
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:09,180
Anybody else or just me?

163
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,900
Okay, cool.

164
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:21,440
But as I came out of that, I literally said to myself, okay, I am going to be a less loving person tonight and tomorrow because of what I just did with my time there.

165
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:25,340
If I want to be a person who demonstrates the love of God, I have to be present to myself.

166
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:30,340
I have to understand what I'm doing with my time and attention and what type of person that is forming me into.

167
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:37,740
We have to be present to God, ourselves, and then finally, that fuels us to be present to others.

168
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,820
We are invited to sacrificially love others.

169
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:43,080
But we should seek to do so from a full tank.

170
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:46,000
The best ministry happens out of the overflow of our heart.

171
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:56,520
Now, that being said, that does not mean that we can say no to a ministry that God is calling us to because we don't feel like it.

172
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:58,280
There's a tension here.

173
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,080
There's a balance here.

174
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:06,500
And I do this because in Mark 6, 34, three verses after the verse where we read, Jesus told his disciples to go take a rest.

175
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:07,520
They needed a rest.

176
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,620
They go on their way to the rest.

177
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:12,720
And again, parents of toddlers will understand this and experience this.

178
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:18,520
On their way to rest, it says this, Jesus saw a huge crowd.

179
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:25,060
And as he stepped from the boat, he had compassion on them because they were like sheep without shepherd.

180
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:26,720
He needed rest.

181
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:28,120
The disciples needed rest.

182
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,900
But the people needed his presence more.

183
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:31,560
This is the tension, right?

184
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:38,220
How do we decide when we need to rest and when we need to just, by the power of the Holy Spirit, go and do what God's calling us to do?

185
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:40,160
Holy Spirit is the short answer.

186
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:41,180
We can figure that out later.

187
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:48,740
Followers of Jesus were invited to sacrificially serve others the way Jesus has loved us so that the world can know that God's love for them.

188
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:51,100
1 John 3, 16, my favorite verse for weddings.

189
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:55,620
We know what real love is because Jesus gave up his life for us.

190
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:59,820
So we also ought to sacrificially give up our lives for our brothers and sisters.

191
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:05,340
Because Jesus sacrificially loved us, we can go and sacrificially love others.

192
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,240
I think I'm doing really great.

193
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:09,680
Yes.

194
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:20,220
I know this seems like a daunting task, but the good news is that this job, our job, to be sacrificially present to those around us, it's a temp job.

195
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:22,580
Anybody ever had a temp job before?

196
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:23,580
Right?

197
00:15:23,580 --> 00:15:24,300
It's a temp job.

198
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,080
This isn't permanent.

199
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:35,780
And we're not stuck in this cycle because thirdly and finally, God will fully and eternally reveal his love to the world by his physical presence returning from heaven to earth.

200
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:40,160
The first Advent was just a taste, just a glimpse of God's love for us.

201
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:48,960
And ultimately, it will be fully revealed to us when Christ returns his second coming and sets up his kingdom on earth as it is in heaven for eternity.

202
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:52,920
And then it will be our job just to reflect his love to those around us.

203
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:57,780
The revelation of God's love is being progressively revealed through his sacrificial presence.

204
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:00,820
It was surprisingly revealed through the first Advent.

205
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:08,180
It is being revealed through the presence of the Holy Spirit in the church now, and it will be fully revealed at the second Advent of Jesus.

206
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,240
Again, 1 John.

207
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:15,460
If you want homework this week, just read the book of 1 John, and you will be smacked in the face with the word love over and over and over again.

208
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:22,440
He says, dear friends, we are already God's children, but he has not yet shown us what we will be like when Christ appears.

209
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:29,980
We do not know, but we do know that we will be like him, for we will see him as he really is.

210
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:31,080
Physical presence.

211
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:38,260
And all who have this hope, this eager expectation, will keep themselves pure, just as he is pure.

212
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:43,820
Advent is a season where we look back to the sacrificial presence of Christ through his incarnation.

213
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:50,440
And we seek to be a visible representation of Jesus in this present world through the power of the Holy Spirit,

214
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:56,160
as we look forward with anticipation to the second Advent of Jesus in the future.

215
00:16:56,160 --> 00:17:01,280
Biblical love is most clearly demonstrated through sacrificial presence.

216
00:17:02,280 --> 00:17:06,840
Church, may we be a people who regularly receive God's love through presence with him.

217
00:17:08,260 --> 00:17:16,980
May we extend God's love through sacrificial presence to others as we eagerly await the final revealing of God's love,

218
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:19,740
when his presence will fully return at the second coming.

219
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:20,940
Pray.

220
00:17:22,940 --> 00:17:23,800
Father, I thank you.

221
00:17:23,800 --> 00:17:23,820
Father, I thank you.

222
00:17:23,820 --> 00:17:26,160
I thank you for your love.

223
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:32,860
That you don't just ask us to figure out what the word love means on our own.

224
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:36,780
God, we live in a culture where there's so many different definitions for the word of love.

225
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:40,820
God, there's distortions.

226
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:44,840
The enemy takes what you have created and distorts it.

227
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:49,660
And we embrace these ideas that are kind of like biblical love, but not really.

228
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:55,140
But you demonstrated what biblical love is through your sacrificial presence.

229
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:58,100
May we receive that today.

230
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,620
May we receive that this week.

231
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:03,320
May we be a people that sacrificially get away and receive the love of God,

232
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:07,800
the reckless, overwhelming, never-ending, reckless love of God over us.

233
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:18,080
And may we be willing to take that love that we've received and sacrificially lay that love on the line for those around us in need.

234
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:26,660
God, may we be a people that get to see your kingdom more visibly on earth as it is in heaven through our obedience

235
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,900
and through your supernatural power.

236
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,700
In Jesus' name I pray.

237
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,540
Amen.
